{{Culture of Cartadania}}
'''Healthcare in Cartadania''' and the Cartadanian health care system is, by law, one of universal health care. Funded through a combination of robust government national health insurance and a mixed public-private framework, Cartadania's healthcare system is designed to provide universal coverage. It ranks among the world's best healthcare systems, typicall placing around second place on the World Health Organization's global assessments, just after [[Burgundie]]. Financially, the federal government allocates 6.71% of its GDP to healthcare and human services, with an annual budget surpassing $1.9 trillion, accounting for approximately 21% of the federal budget. This significant investment ensures that nearly 75% of healthcare expenditures are covered by government-funded agencies. Healthcare in Cartadania extends to all, including those grappling with chronic conditions, such as cancer, AIDS, or cystic fibrosis, who receive their care free of charge.

