The '''''Via Levantina''''' ("Levantine Way") was an important [[Pre-modern global trade|pre-modern trade route]] connecting northern [[Levantia]] and the basin of the [[Vandarch]] to the [[Odoneru Ocean]]. The route, with minor variations, was the primary economic corridor to northern Levantia from antiquity until the completion of the [[Grand Vandarch Canal]] in the 20th century. This route brought trade through the Levantine interior to the Vandarch through a series of rivers and portages. The Via Levantina played a significant role not only in the commercial history of the continent but also in its settlement, as many major Levantine cities were established by the [[Adonerii]] as trade posts and colonies along the route. It was also the cornerstone part of the [[Levantine transportation system]].

