The '''History of [[Urcea]] from 1902 to 1943''', sometimes called the '''Restoration Period''' consists of the time period between the restoration of [[House de Weluta]] in 1902 and the end of the [[Second Great War]] with the [[Treaty of Kartika]] in [[1943]]. This period was characterized by Urcea's participation in Levantine affairs for the first time since the end of the [[Second Caroline War]], culminating in its participation in the [[Second Great War]] from 1927 to 1953. During this period, Urcea became a globally recognized {{wp|superpower}}. The first several decades of this period saw Urcea in a period of reconstruction following the [[Red Interregnum]], while the remainder of it was consumed with the nation's involvement in the Second Great War.

