'''Caphiric Catholicism''' comprises {{wp|Christian}} traditions and church families that originally developed during the {{wp|early modern period}} in [[Caphiria]] and adjoining territories. The term does not describe a single communion or religious denomination, though is sometimes used to refer to the theological positions of the historic [[Imperial Church]]. The defining characteristic of Caphiric Catholicism is largely {{wp|liturgy|liturgical}} in nature, with the [[Caphiric Rite]] or variations of it being used in worship services being the major signifier of Caphiric Catholic status.

The major Caphiric Catholic body is the [[Caphiric Church]], though derivations of Caphiric Catholicism exist outside of it, particularly within the {{wp|Latin Church|Latin}} [[Personal Ordinariate of Reconciliation]] and the Protestant [[Ecclesiastical_Assembly_of_Sarpedon#Structure_and_organization|Continental Church]]. 

