===Pre-Latin trade===
The pre-Latin period of Levantia is not well understood by economic historians. Agriculture was prevalent on the continent with many Celts engaging in settled, subsistence agriculture, with urban centers such as [[Caolladania]] emerging as specialization took root. The ''[[Via Levantina]]'' existed before the establishment of the first Latin colonies and was conducted by tribes and realms which served as middle men and merchants along the [[Urce River]] to [[Vandarch]] and beyond, but the character and economic context of these actors is vague.
