'''Alveria''' is a term describing the eastern region of [[Urcea]] surrounding the [[Magnag]]; its etymology is rooted in the [[Lebhan]] word for "basin". It encompasses the provinces of [[Riancastra]], [[Ardthirium]], and [[Niallán]] as well as southern [[Harren]]. Alveria extends out from the Magnag to the surrounding [[Ionian Mountains]] to the north and northwest and the [[Hortus Mountains]] to the southeast. Due to its geographic and topological location, it is considered one of the most temperate and pleasant parts of [[Urcea]], rivaled only by [[Carolina]]. As a result of its accommodating climate, Alveria was the site of significant [[Adonerii]] settlement during the [[Latin Heroic Age]] making it, along with [[The Gold Coast (Urcea)|the Gold Coast]], one of the most predominantly [[Latinic people|Latinic]] influenced parts of Urcea.

