The '''Sellan''' is a ridge in [[Urcea]] which connects the [[Ionian Mountains]] in the northeast and the [[Hortus Mountains]] in the southwest. The Sellan allows for overland travel from [[Gassavelia]] in the southeast to [[Riancastra]] in the northwest via the Sellanar Vale in southeastern Riancastra. Accordingly, it has provided a major connection between [[Alveria]] and the [[Saianda River]] basin since antiquity. A path through the Sellan was part of the [[Levantine transportation system#Overland_roads|Levantine paved road system]] and was known as the ''Via Sellae'', which was an important connection point from the interior of modern Urcea to the ''[[Via Dericanus]]'' during the time of [[Great Levantia]]. Its name in [[Lebhan]] means "the saddle", named both for its appearance and for its connection of these two very important mountain ranges. Unlike the mountains surrounding it, parts of the Sellan are only about 1,700 ft in elevation.

