'''Freeman''', within [[Social class in Urcea|Urcea's traditional class system]], was a class describing those not [[Feudalism in Urcea|held as feudal serfs]] but nonetheless not possessing the legal rights and privileges of [[Optimate (Urcea)|optimates]] or the [[privilegiata]]. In early Urcea, freemen were the most common type of person in medieval Urcea. Not possessing enough land to be vested or an optimate, freemen nonetheless were under no feudal obligation and worked as a kind of sharecropper or in cities. Possessing no privileges or benefits, the rights of a freeman were nonetheless inviolable and they could not be bought or sold at will, and contracted their labor on their own.

